From c70e6be47dfa455db0ce87c136e969476186f0da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 15:35:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0144 -- wave-49 H-A mds_clear LUT swap

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-49-MDS-CLEAR-DESIGN.md: per-row
coverage LUT (240 bytes; 1 byte per screen-row) that skips the
SDL_memset for rows guaranteed to be fully BG-covered by the BG tile
layer that renders right after clearScreen. Bytes-eliminated
bandwidth-bound lever (sec. 2.2 of design doc); architectural
pressure-test of whether bandwidth-bound levers escape the wave-48
cache-cost-matches-render-cost pattern.

LEVER MECHANISM:
- At map load (or any time map.tiles[][] mutates), walk the full map
  width per row + aggregate via per-screen-Y scroll-range mapping.
- LUT[sy] = 0 (skip) iff ALL map rows reachable at screen-Y sy have
  zero tile-0 columns. LUT[sy] = 1 (clear) otherwise.
- Lazy rebuild on map change OR tile mutation; explicit invalidate
  hooks at the two mutation sites in the codebase.
- DrawScene-scoped per-call signal gates the LUT dispatch path;
  non-DrawScene clearScreen callers (title, save-select, mods menu,
  end-game island, ScreenEffects flash) fall through to legacy full
  memset because their BG tile layer doesn't subsequently render to
  overwrite skipped rows.

STOP-AND-ACK TRIGGER MITIGATIONS integrated (nx-engine wave-49 audit
per flush-instr design contract sec. 6):
- Trigger 1 (dynamic tile mutation): invalidate hooks at
  map_ChangeTileWithSmoke (called from Heavypress boss + Balrog
  cutscene + every AI tile-destroy) AND TSC <CMP at tsc.cpp:1062
  (every scripted door-open / floor-reveal event). Lazy rebuild on
  next clearScreen call after invalidate; ~76800 compares per
  rebuild = negligible at TSC event cadence.
- Trigger 2 (non-DrawScene clearScreen callers): per-call signal
  via static flag set by DrawScene immediately before MdsClearTimer
  scope, cleared immediately after. Renderer::clearScreen INDEX8
  path checks the flag; only DrawScene-originated clears use the
  LUT dispatch. Five non-DrawScene call sites identified in audit
  (intro/title.cpp:66/367/387, pause/mods.cpp:75, endgame/island.
  cpp:83, screeneffect.cpp:44/173) all naturally fall to legacy
  full memset.
- Trigger 3 (tile-ID 0 semantics): cleared via wave-34 patch 0130
  documentation at map.cpp:126 ("tile_id 0 in Cave Story is the
  'empty' tile -- no FG/BG draw -> backdrop pixel reaches the
  composited framebuffer"). Canonical reuse; same conservatism
  basis as wave-34's _build_bg_visible_table.

FILES (~250 LOC total; ~70 LOC substantive + ~180 LOC comments per
the design's essential-correctness-doc convention):
- src/map.h: API decls + correctness model docs (44 lines)
- src/map.cpp: file-scope state + helpers + invalidation hook in
  map_ChangeTileWithSmoke (165 lines)
- src/graphics/Renderer.cpp: clearScreen INDEX8 path per-row
  dispatch (32 lines)
- src/game.cpp: DrawScene per-call signal set/reset (12 lines)
- src/tsc.cpp: <CMP opcode invalidation hook (9 lines)

KILLSWITCH: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MDS_CLEAR_LUT=0 (strict-0 match;
default ON). Cached static-const-bool on first call; subsequent
calls hit the cache. Per BOOT.md convention.

PREDICTED OUTCOMES (per `[[perf_measurement_discipline]]`):
- Canonical Mimiga scene: hypothesis 70% rows skippable
  (sky regions clear; floor + walls skip). Bandwidth savings
  ~54 KB / clearScreen call = ~1.6 ms saved at PODP83 17 MB/s
  sysmem write speed.
- Average across multi-scene TAS: -1 to -2 ms / flip = +0.5 to
  +1.5 fps on the wave-48 30.02 fps baseline.
- Architectural verdict at PLAY3 vs PLAY4 fps A/B: bandwidth-
  bound levers viable vs absorbed-pattern. See
  WAVE-49-MDS-CLEAR-DESIGN sec. 5.

CORRECTNESS REASONING (per design sec. 2.3 + audit):
- Skip-row pixels retain prior frame content; BG tile layer
  subsequently overwrites EVERY pixel in those rows because by LUT
  definition every column has tile != 0 in some reachable scroll
  position.
- Static analysis bound holds so long as map.tiles[][] doesn't
  mutate; mutation invalidation hooks (trigger 1) cover the
  failure mode.
- Visual A/B at build-qa smoke is essential per design sec. 6
  trigger 5: any residual prior-frame pixels in nominally-cleared
  areas = static analysis bug somewhere.

Single-mechanism preserved per
[[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_impossible]]:
the lever is "per-row skip-clear via static BG-coverage LUT". NO
ride-along correctness patches in this iter. NO audio code
touched. NO wave-48 bg-skip code paths modified.

Banner regex for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS:
"map: mds_clear LUT (ENABLED \(default\)|DISABLED \(killswitch\))"
"mds-clear-lut: rebuilt N=\d+ entries \(k_skip=\d+% k_keep=\d+%"
