+// DOS-PORT (patch 0144, Phase 11 wave 49 H-A mds_clear LUT swap):
+// per-row coverage LUT that skips the SDL_memset for rows guaranteed
+// to be fully BG-covered. The lever attacks bandwidth-bound bytes-
+// written cost (rather than wave-48's cache-substitute pattern) per
+// docs/internal/WAVE-49-MDS-CLEAR-DESIGN.md.
+//
+// Correctness model (per flush-instr design contract sec. 2.3 + nx-
+// engine wave-49 audit):
+//   - LUT is built from the static map.tiles[][] data; rows where the
+//     FULL MAP across all reachable scroll positions has at least one
+//     tile == 0 column are marked "exposable" (must clear); rows where
+//     ALL columns are tile != 0 are marked "skippable."
+//   - LUT is INVALIDATED on any runtime tile mutation (TSC <CMP, AI
+//     map_ChangeTileWithSmoke) -- after invalidate, the next
+//     clearScreen path triggers rebuild lazily. This catches Heavypress
+//     floor-break, Balrog cutscene, every door-open scripted event.
+//   - LUT dispatch is gated on a per-call "dispatch eligible" flag set
+//     by DrawScene's MdsClearTimer scope only. Other clearScreen call
+//     sites (title, save-select, mods menu, end-game island, screen
+//     effects) fall through to legacy full-screen memset because their
+//     BG tile layer doesn't subsequently render to overwrite the
+//     skipped rows.
+//
+// API:
+//   - map_mds_clear_lut_invalidate(): called from tile-mutation sites.
+//   - map_mds_clear_lut_ensure_built(): lazy rebuild; called from
+//     Renderer::clearScreen INDEX8 path before LUT consultation.
+//   - map_mds_clear_lut_set_dispatch_eligible(bool): DrawScene flips
+//     the per-call signal on/off around the MdsClearTimer scope.
+//   - map_mds_clear_lut_dispatch_eligible(): Renderer reads the
+//     per-call signal.
+//   - map_mds_clear_lut_should_skip_row(int sy): returns true iff this
+//     screen-row is statically-covered and the memset can be skipped.
+void map_mds_clear_lut_invalidate();
+void map_mds_clear_lut_ensure_built();
+void map_mds_clear_lut_set_dispatch_eligible(bool eligible);
+bool map_mds_clear_lut_dispatch_eligible();
+bool map_mds_clear_lut_should_skip_row(int sy);
+
 void map_flush_graphics();
 void map_drawwaterlevel(void);
 void map_draw(uint8_t foreground);
